 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dfo-7-YyVA4/",
 "title": "Cold Calling Mistakes Based on Data",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "The creator shares three common cold calling mistakes based on a study of over 90,000 recorded cold calls by Chris. The main lesson is to treat prospects as equals, avoid negative opening questions, and keep the introduction fast without pausing.",
 "key_points": [
  "Do not address the prospect as 'sir' or 'ma'am' because it gives them authority; address them by their first name and talk to them like an equal.",
  "Do not use negative opening questions such as 'Did I catch you at a bad time?', as sentences with this phrasing have a success rate of less than 1%.",
  "Do not pause during the initial seconds of the call; the first 10 seconds define a cold call, so introduce yourself and the company immediately and keep moving.",
  "Based on Chris's study of 90,000+ recorded cold calls, successful cold calls have a longer average monologue duration.",
  "Successful cold calls talk 54% and listen 46% of the time, whereas unsuccessful cold calls talk 62% and listen 38% of the time."
 ],
 "content": "Text on screen: finding cold calling difficult? [unclear] Finding cold calling difficult? Here are a few places be going wrong. I went through Chris's study on 90,000 plus recorded cold calls and here are my takeaways. First, do not address the prospect as sir or ma'am. It feels polite, but it gives them the authority. Address them with their first name and treat them and talk to them like an equal. Second is do not use negations. Did I catch you at a bad time? You've basically handed over the opportunity for them to say, yes, okay, bye. In Chris's study, these sentences have a success rate of lesser than 1%. Third, do not pause during the initial seconds. Your first 10 seconds define your cold call. So introduce yourself, introduce the company and start and keep moving on. I've collated all of these observations into a brief PDF. If you need these observations, just comment down cold call and I'll send you these. [unclear] Text on screen: Don't Be Afraid to Monologue: Successful cold calls have a longer average monologue duration. Talk More: Tap into 'ours' of the conversation. Successful Calls: Talk 54%, Listen 46%. Unsuccessful Calls: Talk 62%, Listen 38%. Duration of Cold Call: Successful Calls: 5:50. Unsuccessful Calls: 3:14. Caption: Some important cold calling tips. #fyp #sales #strategy #talk #reality",
 "status": "done",
